  "hypothesis": "A stable bottom-up merge sort and a run-length mode scan exploit the existing contiguous column layout, replacing quadratic work with sequential passes over each column.",
  "notes": "The reusable scratch buffer is freed after sorting. Columns containing NaN retain the original bubble-sort ordering and use a global-count mode fallback; unavailable scratch also falls back to bubble sort. Mode counts are initialized deterministically.",
